      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, intermittent \"wave-like\" issues that persist after physical cable swaps often indicate external electromagnetic interference (EMI) or a random, rare hardware glitch. Since the issue disappears after rebooting or replacing hardware, it rules out a persistent static routing configuration or a permanent loopback configuration error. I recommend using a spectrum analyzer to monitor radio frequency noise on the line during the outage windows to confirm EMI.",
