    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the tip about the spectrum analyzer. one of the senior techs mentioned that this kind of \"ghost in the machine\" stuff used to be called a \"gremlin\" back in the day. just curious—aside from EMI or hardware failure, is there anything else that could cause this kind of unpredictable, erratic behavior in the packets?",
