      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, other potential causes include a misconfigured Quality of Service (QoS) policy or rate limiter causing intermittent bandwidth throttling, or a rogue device generating traffic bursts that overload the local switch. You might also consider checking physical layer errors (CRC errors) on the router interfaces, as these often spike only under heavy load before dropping packets entirely. Another possibility is a faulty firmware version on the edge router that triggers memory leaks or packet drops under specific network conditions.",
